## (a) Green's function via method of images

The operator is $L = \partial_t^2 - c^2\partial_x^2$ on the half-line $x>0$ with homogeneous Dirichlet data $u(0,t)=0$ (the boundary driving $h(t)$ is handled separately in part (b) by lifting to a particular solution). The retarded Green's function $G_D(x,t;\xi,\tau)$ satisfies

$$L G_D = \delta(x-\xi)\delta(t-\tau),\qquad x,\xi>0,\quad G_D=0\ \text{for}\ t<\tau,\quad G_D(0,t;\xi,\tau)=0.$$

On the **full line** the retarded Green's function for the 1-D wave operator is

$$G_{\text{free}}(x,t;\xi,\tau)=\frac{1}{2c}\,H\!\big(c(t-\tau)-|x-\xi|\big),$$

where $H$ is the Heaviside step function. (One verifies $L G_{\text{free}}=\delta(x-\xi)\delta(t-\tau)$ by differentiating the "tent" of support $|x-\xi|\le c(t-\tau)$; the two jump discontinuities at $x=\xi\pm c(t-\tau)$ each contribute $c$ and the kink at $x=\xi$ contributes the delta in $x$.)

**Method of images.** To enforce $G_D(0,t;\xi,\tau)=0$, place an image source of opposite sign at the reflected point $-\xi$:

$$\boxed{\;G_D(x,t;\xi,\tau)=\frac{1}{2c}\Big[H\!\big(c(t-\tau)-|x-\xi|\big)-H\!\big(c(t-\tau)-|x+\xi|\big)\Big],\qquad x,\xi>0.\;}$$

At $x=0$: $|0-\xi|=|0+\xi|=\xi$, so the two Heaviside factors are identical and cancel, giving $G_D(0,t;\xi,\tau)=0$. The image source lies outside the physical domain ($-\xi<0$), so causality and the PDE inside $x>0$ are preserved. This is the Dirichlet Green's function for the half-line.

The general solution with source $Q$, initial data $f,g$ and **homogeneous** boundary $u(0,t)=0$ is then

$$u(x,t)=\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\!\int_0^\infty\! G_D(x,t;\xi,0)\,f(\xi)\,d\xi+\int_0^\infty\! G_D(x,t;\xi,0)\,g(\xi)\,d\xi+\int_0^t\!\!\int_0^\infty\! G_D(x,t;\xi,\tau)\,Q(\xi,\tau)\,d\xi\,d\tau.$$

